($bc27527$love-friends-07$bc27527$,$bc27528$small_gap_both_content$bc27528$,$bc27529$Case dismissed. Protocols synced.$bc27529$,$bc27530$$bc27530$,$bc27531$You're both running the exact same post-social recovery protocol, same duration, same method, which means neither of you is ever standing around wondering when the other one will be 'done' decompressing. That matched protocol turns recovery time into something you can actually share, side by side, instead of one of you waiting on the other's timeline.$bc27531$,$bc27532$name what your recovery time actually looks like, specifically. same.$bc27532$,$bc27533$Case dismissed. Protocols synced.$bc27533$,$bc27534$Approved v4 template$bc27534$,$bc27535$Unexpected Analogy$bc27535$,$bc27536$$bc27536$,$bc27537$name what your recovery time actually looks like, specifically.$bc27537$,$bc27538$same.$bc27538$,$bc27539$Both of you plan your next post-social downtime together, doing your own version of recharge side by side.$bc27539$,$bc27540$Case dismissed. Protocols synced.$bc27540$),
($bc27541$love-friends-07$bc27541$,$bc27542$small_gap_split$bc27542$,$bc27543$Case dismissed. Permission, granted.$bc27543$,$bc27544$[A] = the partner who indicated it bothers them.$bc27544$,$bc27545$Same recovery need, but [A] feels like they need a permission slip to take it, while [B] never knew one was required in the first place. Once that permission's granted out loud, recovery stops being something [A] has to justify and just becomes something you both already agreed was fine.$bc27545$,$bc27546$name that your recovery time is legitimate, out loud. reassure once, specifically, that the timing's genuinely fine.$bc27546$,$bc27547$Case dismissed. Permission, granted.$bc27547$,$bc27548$Approved v4 template$bc27548$,$bc27549$Reframe$bc27549$,$bc27550$[A] = the partner who indicated it bothers them.$bc27550$,$bc27551$name that your recovery time is legitimate, out loud.$bc27551$,$bc27552$reassure once, specifically, that the timing's genuinely fine.$bc27552$,$bc27553$Both of you name your actual recovery routines and agree, together, neither one needs to apologize for it.$bc27553$,$bc27554$Case dismissed. Permission, granted.$bc27554$),
