($bc27569$love-friends-07$bc27569$,$bc27570$large_gap_both_content$bc27570$,$bc27571$Case dismissed. Paces, both accounted for.$bc27571$,$bc27572$[A] = needs more recovery; [B] = recovers fast.$bc27572$,$bc27573$[A], your longer recovery isn't low social stamina, it's a marathoner's pacing, you go the distance during the event and need real time to rebuild after. [B], bouncing back fast isn't shallow engagement, it's a sprinter's recovery, quick reset because the effort was spent in a quick, intense burst. Between the two of you, you've got a marathoner and a sprinter under one roof, which means whatever kind of social event comes up, one of your paces is built for it.$bc27573$,$bc27574$name your actual recovery need clearly, this week. give that space fully, without checking in too soon.$bc27574$,$bc27575$Case dismissed. Paces, both accounted for.$bc27575$,$bc27576$Approved v4 template$bc27576$,$bc27577$Unexpected Analogy$bc27577$,$bc27578$[A] = needs more recovery; [B] = recovers fast.$bc27578$,$bc27579$name your actual recovery need clearly, this week.$bc27579$,$bc27580$give that space fully, without checking in too soon.$bc27580$,$bc27581$Both of you plan your next social event with [A]'s recovery time already built into the schedule.$bc27581$,$bc27582$Case dismissed. Paces, both accounted for.$bc27582$),
